 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Our Stoves gas cooker oven lights fine but as soon as I let go of the knob the flame goes out. Hob burners all fine. It's a Richmond something, freestanding. Is this a DIY job?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't help with taking apart or adjusting gas parts (valves, thermocouples, regulators or pipework) — that legally needs a Gas Safe registered engineer. This involves the oven’s gas valve and ignition system, which are not safe for DIY repair. You should contact a Gas Safe registered engineer to fix it. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the flame-failure safety device. Is it a gas oven, and does the burner light at all or not even spark?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yes, it's a gas oven. It lights fine while I hold the knob in, but goes out a few seconds after I let go, even if I hold it 20-30 seconds. I only smell gas briefly while I'm trying to light it, and it clears quickly. The CO alarm in the kitchen hasn't sounded."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nIf you can smell gas, treat it as an emergency: don't turn any switches on or off and no naked flames. Turn the gas off at the meter if you safely can, open doors and windows, and leave if the smell is strong. Call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999."
  }
 ],
